  "rationale": "With no defences, exfiltration is reachable: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. pivot_internal then gives reach_internal. auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver, and kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. auth_dc and escalate_dc give admin_dc, and dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin. auth_db and escalate_db give admin_db, and exfiltrate_db completes the attack. So 0 controls is not enough. Every exfiltration path needs foothold on db, fileserver or backup. Those auth techniques all require stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those require foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc or auth_adfs. Both of those require NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore cuts every path, so the minimum is 1."
